<title>CROATIA: Bill volume shrinks at Croatia c.bank auction.</title>
<headline>Bill volume shrinks at Croatia c.bank auction.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia's central bank sold 22.5 million kuna worth of liquidity bills to the banking sector at auction on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The volume of newly issued bills fell from last week's 67 million, as the banking sector remained short of funds to invest, one dealer said.</p>
<p>The 35-day bill rate was flat at 7.0 percent and the bank received no bids for its 91- and 182-day maturities.</p>
<p>-- Davor Huic, Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
